WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.660
Before you build the whole thing,

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:03.840
decide what would make
it worth building.

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:07.580
One Small Venture helps you choose
a practical route and build a

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:09.120
fourteen-day test plan.

00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:12.020
Start with fifteen
questions about your time,

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:16.300
skills, preferences, buyer
access, and practical limits.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:20.860
You'll compare four possible routes and
see how your answers shaped the suggestion.

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:23.960
For example: a reusable workflow kit.

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:26.460
Instead of making an entire library,

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:29.760
start with one checklist
for one specific task.

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:31.620
Name the person it could help.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:33.740
Set your time and spending caps.

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:35.900
Then write down what you'll observe,

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:37.660
and what would make you continue,

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:39.640
change direction, or stop.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:43.860
The quiz doesn't validate demand
or promise a successful business.

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:46.800
It helps you choose what
to investigate next.

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:50.960
Your worksheet is editable, so you can
make the plan fit your circumstances,

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:52.960
save it, and put it to work.

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:55.800
Try the free One Small Venture quiz.

00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:58.220
Leave with one experiment
you can explain,

00:00:58.220 --> 00:01:00.940
and a next step you can take.
